### 6.2 Simulation context
File: src/context/SimulationContext.jsx

This is the most important frontend state engine.

Local scenario dataset:
- 12 phishing templates (varied social engineering themes)
- 6 legitimate templates (normal internal messages)

State and refs:
- simulationState: IDLE, RUNNING, COMPLETED
- inbox and selected email
- session object with interaction log
- open-timestamp tracking for hesitation metrics
- refs for resolved email ids, used templates, fetch lock, live session/inbox

Main methods:
- startSimulation()
  - resets refs
  - builds profile snapshot from user profile
  - generates initial 3 emails (API-first)
  - initializes session

- generateEmails(count, profile)
  - POST http://localhost:5000/api/generate-emails
  - falls back to local template pool if backend unavailable/fails

- refillInbox()
  - if unresolved/pending drops below 3, auto-add 2 or 3 emails
  - keeps pending capped (skip if already >= 9)

- markAsRead(id)
  - marks email read
  - records first-open timestamp

- logInteraction(type, details)
  - computes hesitationMs from open timestamp
  - appends interaction to session

- loadNextEmail(resolvedId)
  - marks an email resolved
  - advances selection to next unresolved
  - triggers refill check

- calculateRisk(interactions)
  - VERY_HIGH if credentials entered
  - HIGH if fake link clicked
  - MEDIUM if legit link clicked
  - LOW if phishing reported or no severe failures

- endSimulation({deferNavigation})
  - computes final risk + avg hesitation
  - saves partial result immediately to localStorage (fast dashboard load)
  - optionally sets simulation state to COMPLETED
  - requests explanation from backend (/api/generate-explanation)
  - updates localStorage entry with final explanation
  - saves final session to Firestore if uid available

