## 13. Runtime data flows (end-to-end)

### 13.1 Simulation run flow
1) User starts at /simulation
2) SimulationContext starts session and requests initial emails
3) User actions are logged with timestamps and hesitation
4) endSimulation computes risk + avg hesitation
5) Partial result saved to localStorage immediately
6) Explanation requested from backend
7) localStorage session updated with explanation
8) Firestore session persisted (if authenticated)
9) Dashboard reads and visualizes results

### 13.2 Threat generator flow
1) User opens /training/threat-generator
2) Categories loaded from backend
3) Threat generated from Gemini or local fallback
4) User can save threat briefing to Firestore
5) User can improve existing threat and update cloud record

### 13.3 Auth/profile personalization flow
1) User signs in
2) createUserProfile ensures users/{uid} exists
3) Profile loaded into AuthContext
4) Profile details edited in Profile page
5) Simulation uses profile snapshot for personalized generation and explanation

## 14. Important implementation strengths

- Strong fallback-first design:
  - Simulation can still work without Gemini
  - Dashboard can still work without Firestore (localStorage fallback)

- Profile-aware simulation personalization:
  - Prompts and fallback templates adapt to user context

- Behavioral analytics:
  - Tracks what users did and how quickly they decided

- Multiple learning channels:
  - realistic desktop simulation
  - guided scenario drills
  - gamified challenge
  - AI threat briefing generation

## 15. Notable implementation notes

- The simulation infrastructure is designed to avoid stale closure issues by pairing React state with mutable refs for current session/inbox snapshots.
- The backend consistently strips markdown fences from Gemini output and validates JSON before using it.
- Taskbar currently references activeWindow from window manager context, while WindowManager does not expose activeWindow explicitly; taskbar active highlighting may therefore not behave as intended unless derived from z-index/open state.

